condition reveals a strong majority class bias driving most failures. Across models, exception_only errors show the most consistency in which samples fail, indicating those are genuinely irreducible cases, whereas full_trace and no_trace errors are more model-specific.\n\nNow I'm organizing the tables and figures—error mode distributions, error rates by trace length, and cross-model overlap patterns—along with confusion matrices for each condition. I need to make sure the narrative captures how all seven planned experiments confirm the pattern exists but varies significantly by model strength, with stronger models showing gradual phase transitions while weaker ones exhibit sharper transitions. 使 'universal sharp phase transition' 降级为 'consistent trend with model-dependent transition characteristics'。plan_017 (cross-seed) 的 std 范围 0.4-3.5pp 证明 budget curve 本身 reproducible 但 variance 与模型强度相关。plan_019 (calibration) 确认 exception_only 的 near-perfect calibration 跨 4 模型通用（非离群 ECE ≤ 0.01）。plan_020 (few-shot) 确认 SFT 优于 frontier model few-shot 3-5pp, 支持 SFT 作为 practical recommendation 但不是压倒性优势。plan_018 (error analysis) 和 plan_022 (training dynamics) 提供 supporting evidence 但不升级任何 claim。plan_021 (OOD) 是最大风险——跨语言泛化可能大幅降级。总体：Claim 1 + Claim 3 的核心证据不受影响, budget curve 保留为 supporting evidence, EMNLP main 有竞争力 (P=0.35-0.45) 但 scope concern + model-dependent phase transition 需要 strong rebuttal 应对。现在要整理 YAML，需要先确认 Qwen-7B tail-256 的数值——两个实验记录中一个是 77.48%，另一个是 78.9%，得核实哪个是正确的版本。 The difference might be due to different truncation methods, so I'll use 78.9% as the canonical value since it's from the more recent experiment. Now I need to think through what plan_020 should predict—specifically whether to test GPT-4o and Claude with no trace input as a non-SFT upper bound, comparing 0-shot and 3-shot performance on exception_only traces. I'm estimating GPT-4o with exception traces at around 96% accuracy and without traces at roughly 83%, which would demonstrate that even frontier models gain